{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779065064,"nonce":"GIrO2JBv/2i7E6W/PSFTtmWU6nM=","title":"Phase 4b: route Studio train scenarios through provider execution contract","message":"## Parent / coordination\n- Roadmap: `fa3978f` — Feedbax/Mandible MVP integration roadmap.\n- Workspace foundation: `b424865`.\n- Pipeline workspace spec: `0c46f69`.\n- Provider/execution contract: `c6b1b73`.\n- Later real JAX training backend: `e57ae1f`.\n\n## Problem\nThe first Studio workspace slice adds durable train/eval/analysis/report scenarios, but local Studio execution is still not bound to the Feedbax provider execution contract. If Studio launches work directly from legacy stores or hidden frontend state, the workspace model and provider contract can drift before the MVP is fully built.\n\n## Scope\nBuild the next additive slice that converts the active train-stage scenario into a provider execution request/plan and exposes enough UI/status/artifact plumbing to prove the path without pretending full cloud or real-JAX training is done.\n\nThe slice should:\n- Add a backend-owned lowering path from `StudioWorkspaceSpec` / active train scenario to an `ExecutionSpec` for local execution.\n- Preserve room for SSH, RunPod, and Modal by using the existing provider-neutral execution contract rather than a Studio-only shortcut.\n- Add API and frontend client/store hooks so Studio can validate/prepare the execution plan from the active workspace state.\n- Attach execution status, manifest refs, artifact refs, or plan refs back to the workspace/stage model in an additive way.\n- Surface a minimal user-facing action/status path in Studio using existing panels where possible.\n- Add tests proving scenario lowering, plan creation, and workspace status/ref updates.\n\n## Non-goals\n- Do not implement live RunPod/Modal submission here.\n- Do not replace the fake/stub training worker with full real JAX training in this slice; that remains `e57ae1f`.\n- Do not introduce a parallel frontend-only execution interpretation path.\n- Do not narrow stage specs to training-only assumptions that would block eval, analysis, report, or cloud execution later.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Given a saved/restored Studio workspace with an active train stage, Feedbax can derive and validate a provider execution plan for local execution.\n- The frontend can request that plan from the active workspace and persist the resulting plan/status references on the train stage.\n- Existing project compatibility remains intact.\n- Tests cover lowering, API behavior, and preservation of future/custom stage metadata.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}